  "variants_tried_note": "8 pre-registered grid cells plus 17 ablations/neighbours and one placebo family are counted here; roughly 120 daily-bar diagnostic backtests across lookbacks, vol targets, vol windows and state rules preceded the frozen 1-minute grid. See report.md section 1.",
  "verdict_note": "Passes the pre-registered development bar (41.15% CAGR, 57.95% max DD). The result is not all-weather: the 2018 Q4 drawdown is essentially a full TQQQ drawdown, 2016-2019 underperforms TQQQ, and the 252-session lookback is load-bearing (126/189 fail). The edge is concentrated in 2019-2020 and in avoiding 2022. See report.md section 6.",
  "caveats": [
    "The 58% max drawdown is the 2018-08-30 to 2018-12-24 TQQQ drawdown (-58.6% in the panel); the 12-month gate and the 85% vol threshold did not de-risk in time. It clears the 60% target by about 2 pp, not by crash protection.",
    "2016-2019 strategy CAGR is below TQQQ's (38.9% vs 49.0%) with the same 58% drawdown. The edge is 2020-2023.",
    "2023 is +42.3% vs TQQQ +198.4%: the 12-month gate re-entered only after the first-half rebound.",
    "Lookback neighbours 126 and 189 fail (31.9% and 28.0% CAGR); the 252-session plateau is narrow in the lookback dimension.",
